Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:32:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 32/70] render: bloom follows its settings live and is tinted

WE re-applies general.bloomstrength, bloomthreshold and bloomtint to the
bloom materials (GH 0x1401b42b0); the LDR chain's downsample shader reads
g_BloomTint ("1 1 1" by default).

The bloom passes' constants were JSON literals taken while the scene was
built, so a user property (or animation) on them did nothing, and
bloomtint was never parsed. They are now connected to the scene's values
(bloomtint parsed, default 1 1 1). The bloom image is built when bloom
is on at load or bound to a user property, and the render loop skips it
while bloom is off (read every frame), so turning bloom on after load
works; it used to exist only when bloom was on at load. A bloom chain
that can't be built (no WE assets) is logged and left out.

Not done: general settings driven by a SceneScript (no script host for
them yet), HDR bloom.

Origin: ours
Why: bloom ignored its tint and every change after load (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B9: E36, E37)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8a42pVTGcB74tx4LjJ
